  "question": {
    "text": "Van der Waal&#39;s equation for a gas is stated as,<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>P</mtext><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mtext>nRT</mtext><mrow><mtext>V</mtext><mo>-</mo><mtext>nb</mtext></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mtext>a</mtext><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mtext>n</mtext><mtext>V</mtext></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math>.<br /><br />This equation reduces to the perfect gas equation, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>P</mtext><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mtext>nRT</mtext><mtext>V</mtext></mfrac></math>&nbsp;When,"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "temperature is sufficiently high and pressure is low.",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "both temperature and pressure are very low.",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "both temperature and pressure are very high.",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "temperature is sufficiently low and pressure is high.",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>At very high temperatures &amp; low pressures, the characteristic constant&nbsp;behaviour can be understood from virial&nbsp;expansion<br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mtext>Z</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>PV</mtext> <mtext>m</mtext> </msub> </mrow> <mrow> <mtext>RT</mtext> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>=</mo> <mn>1</mn> <mo>+</mo> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mtext>b</mtext> <mo>-</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mtext>a</mtext> </mrow> <mrow> <mtext>RT</mtext> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </mfenced> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>V</mtext> <mtext>m</mtext> </msub> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>+</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <msup> <mtext>b</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msup> </mrow> <mrow> <msubsup> <mtext>V</mtext> <mtext>m</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msubsup> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>+</mo> <mtext>....</mtext> </mrow> </math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></msub></math>, molar volume large i.e&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <msup> <mtext>b</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msup> </mrow> <mrow> <msubsup> <mtext>V</mtext> <mtext>m</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msubsup> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>&#8594;</mo> <mtext>o</mtext> </mrow> </math><br /><br />i.e Third term in virial expansion can be ignored.</p><p>In qualitative terms, the real gas will show ideal behaviour when the intermolecular forces of attraction will be negligible which is possible at high temperature and low pressure.<br />Also&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mtext>b</mtext> <mo>-</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mtext>a</mtext> </mrow> <mrow> <mtext>RT</mtext> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </mfenced> <mo>&#8594;</mo> <mtext>o</mtext> </mrow> </math><br /><br />i.e.&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <mtext>Z</mtext> <mo>&#8776;</mo> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;and gas behaves ideally.</p>"
  }
